<title>USA: US won't soften demands on China WTO entry - Rubin.</title>
<headline>US won't soften demands on China WTO entry - Rubin.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The United States is not prepared to soften its basic demands that China agree to open up its markets to imports before being allowed into the World Trade Organization, Treasury Secretary Robert Rubin said on Thursday.</p>
<p>But he said Washington was willing to give Beijing time to carry out some market-opening measures once it has agreed to the U.S. principles.</p>
</text>
